From 0127819cbbc601bd396bea50e5a3e22146d621e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:29:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 45/79] demux: wav: fix wrong pts after a seek

Control() is a bare demux_vaControlHelper() call, and the helper implements
DEMUX_SET_POSITION and DEMUX_SET_TIME as a plain vlc_stream_Seek(): the
stream moves, but the pts accumulator is left untouched and keeps counting
from where it was before the seek.

DEMUX_GET_TIME goes through the same helper and is derived from the byte
offset, so it stays correct, and the timestamps the demuxer emits no longer
agree with the time it reports. Playback of the track itself survives
because the input resets the PCR on every seek, but slave ES do not:
SlaveDemux() paces external subtitles from the master DEMUX_GET_TIME, so
after a seek they are shifted by the accumulated error, or dropped for
being too late or too early.

Resync the date with the new offset, using the same byte to time conversion
as the helper.

Adapted from 7bad2a867f01786ace2e8ff074e5dcc19fb96063: here the date holds
a pts relative to VLC_TICK_0, not an absolute one, and the origin the date
is initialized with has to be kept so that an offset of 0 still yields the
very same pts as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/wav.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/wav.c b/modules/demux/wav.c
index 76197342ae..b2ed38ec16 100644
--- a/modules/demux/wav.c
+++ b/modules/demux/wav.c
@@ -515,10 +515,37 @@ static int Control( demux_t *p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
     if( p_sys->i_data_size > 0 )
         i_end = p_sys->i_data_pos + p_sys->i_data_size;
 
-    return demux_vaControlHelper( p_demux->s, p_sys->i_data_pos, i_end,
-                                   p_sys->fmt.i_bitrate,
-                                   p_sys->fmt.audio.i_blockalign,
-                                   i_query, args );
+    int i_ret = demux_vaControlHelper( p_demux->s, p_sys->i_data_pos, i_end,
+                                       p_sys->fmt.i_bitrate,
+                                       p_sys->fmt.audio.i_blockalign,
+                                       i_query, args );
+    if( i_ret != VLC_SUCCESS )
+        return i_ret;
+
+    switch( i_query )
+    {
+        case DEMUX_SET_POSITION:
+        case DEMUX_SET_TIME:
+        {
+            /* The helper only moved the stream: resync the pts accumulator,
+             * else it would keep counting from before the seek and drift
+             * away from the byte derived DEMUX_GET_TIME. */
+            uint64_t i_ofs = vlc_stream_Tell( p_demux->s );
+            if( unlikely(i_ofs < (uint64_t)p_sys->i_data_pos) )
+                break;
+            i_ofs -= p_sys->i_data_pos;
+
+            /* Same byte to time conversion as demux_vaControlHelper(), kept
+             * relative to the origin the date was initialized with. */
+            date_Set( &p_sys->pts,
+                      1 + INT64_C(8000000) * i_ofs / p_sys->fmt.i_bitrate );
+            break;
+        }
+        default:
+            break;
+    }
+
+    return VLC_SUCCESS;
 }
 
